General design

Two separate experiments were performed, the main one dealing with conversation and the other dealing with dialling. The same individuals participated in both. The experimental design was mixed—half the participant group was tested with and without handsfree phone use, and the other half was tested with and without handheld phone use (for a complete description of the design and other details of the study, see Kircher et al., 2004).
